IMPORT prelude

-- Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Queensland) -- what the other modules share: the dates, the one
-- regulative vocabulary, and the Act's own definitions a claimant meets first: capacity and impaired capacity (sch 4),
-- the presumption of capacity (s 11), financial, personal and legal matters (sch 2 ss 1, 2, 18), paid carer (sch 4).
--
-- SEAT: the adult whose capacity for a claim is in question -- for example a person injured at work or on the road
-- whose compensation claim, settlement or damages award may be managed by an administrator. For ss 60 and 60C the seat
-- is a person who takes from that adult's estate; for ss 247-247C, a person who reports abuse of an adult. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Dates: the prelude's built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY,
-- DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. READINGS (the Act does not say how to count; the Acts
-- Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld) is not deposited and was not read): "within n months after" a day ends on the same day
-- number n months on, or the last day of a shorter month; "within 28 days after" a day ends on that day plus 28; "at
-- least 7 days before the hearing" is met by notice given on the hearing day minus 7 or earlier; an age of "17 1/2
-- years" is reached 210 months after birth. No extension for a day the registry is closed. Forks F1-F4 in NOTES.md.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Guardianship and Administration Act 2000: shared dates, rules and definitions`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `Dates`
-- ===================================================================================================================

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`n` `days after` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`n` `days before` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` MINUS `n`)

GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days from` `the start` `until` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `first` `is on or before` `second` IF DATE_SERIAL `first` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `second`

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `first` `and` `second` MEANS
    IF `first` `is on or before` `second`
    THEN `second`
    ELSE `first`

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` `first` `and` `second` MEANS
    IF `first` `is on or before` `second`
    THEN `first`
    ELSE `second`

-- The number of days in month m of year y.
GIVEN `m` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of month` `m` `y` MEANS
    IF `m` EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_DAY (DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (`m` PLUS 1) `y`) MINUS 1))

-- "n months after" a day (n a whole number, 0 or more): the same day number n months on, or the last day of that month
-- where it is shorter (31 August plus 6 months is 28 or 29 February; a birthday on 29 February falls on 28 February in
-- a common year).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`n` `months after` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the day number` `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `months from January` MEANS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `the new month` MEANS (`months from January` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the new year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS ((`months from January` MINUS (`months from January` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the day number` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the day` AT MOST `the last day of month` `the new month` `the new year`
            THEN DATE_DAY `the day`
            ELSE `the last day of month` `the new month` `the new year`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `The regulative vocabulary (ss 21(1), 59(5)-(6), 60C(4))`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- The parties and acts of the three duties with a numbered deadline encoded as regulative rules. Section 21(1) is the
-- administrator's duty; ss 59(5)-(6) and 60C(4) are the applicant's own time limits ("must be made ... within 6
-- months"). The rules are in gaq-appointment.l4 and gaq-administrator.l4.
DECLARE `Guardianship party` IS ONE OF
    `the administrator`
    `the applicant`

DECLARE `Guardianship act` IS ONE OF
    `advise the registrar of titles of the appointment`
    `apply for compensation or an account of profits`
    `apply to confirm or vary the operation of s 60A`

-- Runs a rule over "the act was done at this time" and answers whether it was done in time. On the stable l4 a
-- CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the party` IS A `Guardianship party`
      `the act` IS A `Guardianship act`
      `the time` IS A NUMBER
      `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Guardianship party` `Guardianship act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the party` `doing` `the act` `at` `the time` `is in time under` `the rule` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time`), (EVENT `the party` `the act` `the time`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The four states of a step with a deadline.
DECLARE `Is the step in time` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it was done within the period the Act allows`
    `no: it was done, but after the period the Act allows had ended`
    `not yet due: it has not been done, but the period has not ended`
    `overdue: the period the Act allows has ended and it has not been done`

GIVEN `the act` IS A `Guardianship act`
      `the party` IS A `Guardianship party`
      `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Guardianship party` `Guardianship act`
      `the day the period starts` IS A DATE
      `it has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was done` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Is the step in time`
`the state of` `the act` `by` `the party` `under` `the rule` `from` `the day the period starts` `done` `it has been done` `on` `the day it was done` `as at` `today` MEANS
    IF `it has been done`
    THEN IF `the party` `doing` `the act` `at` (`the number of days from` `the day the period starts` `until` `the day it was done`) `is in time under` `the rule`
         THEN `yes: it was done within the period the Act allows`
         ELSE `no: it was done, but after the period the Act allows had ended`
    ELSE IF `the party` `doing` `the act` `at` (`the number of days from` `the day the period starts` `until` `today`) `is in time under` `the rule`
         THEN `not yet due: it has not been done, but the period has not ended`
         ELSE `overdue: the period the Act allows has ended and it has not been done`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `Schedule 4 -- capacity and impaired capacity`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- Sch 4: "capacity, for a person for a matter, means the person is capable of-- (a) understanding the nature and effect
-- of decisions about the matter; and (b) freely and voluntarily making decisions about the matter; and (c) communicating
-- the decisions in some way." "impaired capacity, for a person for a matter, means the person does not have capacity
-- for the matter." A "means" definition with three limbs joined by "and": a person short of any limb lacks capacity.
-- Capacity is for "a matter" (one decision area), not for the person at large. Section 146(3): in deciding limb (c) the
-- tribunal must investigate all reasonable ways of facilitating communication (symbol boards, signing), so the fact is
-- asked as "with any reasonable aid".
GIVEN `I can understand the nature and effect of decisions about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can make decisions about the matter freely and voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can communicate the decisions in some way, with any reasonable aid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch 4 -- capacity for the matter` `I can understand the nature and effect of decisions about the matter` `I can make decisions about the matter freely and voluntarily` `I can communicate the decisions in some way, with any reasonable aid` IF
        `I can understand the nature and effect of decisions about the matter`
    AND `I can make decisions about the matter freely and voluntarily`
    AND `I can communicate the decisions in some way, with any reasonable aid`

DECLARE `Do I have capacity for the matter` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you have capacity for the matter (sch 4, capacity)`
    `no: you have impaired capacity for the matter (sch 4, impaired capacity), as you are not capable of every limb of capacity`

@export Do I have capacity, under the Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld), for a matter such as running or settling my own compensation claim (sch 4, capacity and impaired capacity)?
GIVEN `I can understand the nature and effect of decisions about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you understand the nature and effect of decisions about the matter (for example what settling your claim for a given amount means for you)?
      `I can make decisions about the matter freely and voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you make decisions about the matter freely and voluntarily, without someone else's pressure deciding for you?
      `I can communicate the decisions in some way, with any reasonable aid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you communicate your decisions in some way, including with a reasonable aid such as a symbol board or signing?
GIVETH A `Do I have capacity for the matter`
DECIDE `Do I have capacity for the matter question` IS
    IF `sch 4 -- capacity for the matter` `I can understand the nature and effect of decisions about the matter` `I can make decisions about the matter freely and voluntarily` `I can communicate the decisions in some way, with any reasonable aid`
    THEN `yes: you have capacity for the matter (sch 4, capacity)`
    ELSE `no: you have impaired capacity for the matter (sch 4, impaired capacity), as you are not capable of every limb of capacity`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 11 -- the presumption of capacity`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 11(1): "If, in performing a function or exercising a power under this Act, the tribunal or the court is required to
-- make a decision about an adult's capacity for a matter, the tribunal or the court is to presume the adult has
-- capacity for the matter until the contrary is proven." (2): a guardian or administrator appointed for the matter "is
-- not required to presume the adult has capacity for the matter". (3): if a declaration "that an adult has impaired
-- capacity for a matter is in force, a person or other entity that performs a function or exercises a power under this
-- Act is entitled to rely on the declaration to presume that the adult does not have capacity for the matter."
-- "court" is the Supreme Court (sch 4). Subsection (1) has no exception for a declaration in force; read as: the
-- tribunal or court deciding capacity afresh still starts from the presumption (fork F5).
DECLARE `Who is deciding about my capacity` IS ONE OF
    `the tribunal (QCAT) or the Supreme Court, deciding my capacity for the matter`
    `my guardian or administrator appointed for the matter`
    `another person or body acting under the Act`

DECLARE `What may be presumed about my capacity` IS ONE OF
    `you must be presumed to have capacity for the matter until the contrary is proven (s 11(1))`
    `your guardian or administrator for the matter need not presume you have capacity for it (s 11(2))`
    `they may rely on the declaration that you have impaired capacity for the matter and presume you do not have capacity for it (s 11(3))`
    `s 11 gives this person no presumption either way`

GIVEN `who decides` IS A `Who is deciding about my capacity`
      `a declaration that I have impaired capacity for the matter is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What may be presumed about my capacity`
`s 11 -- the presumption` `who decides` `a declaration that I have impaired capacity for the matter is in force` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who decides`
    WHEN `the tribunal (QCAT) or the Supreme Court, deciding my capacity for the matter` THEN `you must be presumed to have capacity for the matter until the contrary is proven (s 11(1))`
    WHEN `my guardian or administrator appointed for the matter` THEN `your guardian or administrator for the matter need not presume you have capacity for it (s 11(2))`
    WHEN `another person or body acting under the Act` THEN
        IF `a declaration that I have impaired capacity for the matter is in force`
        THEN `they may rely on the declaration that you have impaired capacity for the matter and presume you do not have capacity for it (s 11(3))`
        ELSE `s 11 gives this person no presumption either way`

@export Must the tribunal, the court or my guardian or administrator presume I have capacity for the matter (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 11)?
GIVEN `who decides` IS A `Who is deciding about my capacity` @desc Who is making the decision about your capacity: the tribunal (QCAT) or Supreme Court deciding it; your guardian or administrator appointed for the matter; or another person or body acting under the Act
      `a declaration that I have impaired capacity for the matter is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a declaration by the tribunal or the court that you have impaired capacity for this matter in force?
GIVETH A `What may be presumed about my capacity`
DECIDE `Must my capacity be presumed question` IS
    `s 11 -- the presumption` `who decides` `a declaration that I have impaired capacity for the matter is in force`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `Schedule 2 ss 1, 2, 18 -- is my claim a financial matter or a personal matter?`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- Sch 2 s 1: "A financial matter, for an adult, is a matter relating to the adult's financial or property matters,
-- including, for example, ... (c) receiving and recovering money payable to the adult; ... (o) a legal matter relating to
-- the adult's financial or property matters". s 2: "A personal matter ... is a matter ... relating to the adult's care
-- ... or welfare, including ... (i) a legal matter not relating to the adult's financial or property matter". s 18: "A
-- legal matter, for an adult, includes a matter relating to-- ... (c) use of legal services to bring or defend a
-- proceeding ...; and (d) bringing or defending a proceeding, including settling a claim, whether before or after the
-- start of a proceeding." The two "legal matter" limbs split by whether the claim relates to the adult's financial or
-- property matters: an administrator (financial matter) or a guardian (personal matter). A compensation claim for money
-- is a legal matter relating to financial matters (s 1(c), (o)). "includes" in s 18: a matter outside its heads is not
-- shown to be a legal matter (NOTHING).
DECLARE `Which kind of matter is my claim` IS ONE OF
    `a financial matter: a legal matter relating to your financial or property matters, for an administrator (sch 2 ss 1(o), 18)`
    `a personal matter: a legal matter not relating to your financial or property matters, for a guardian (sch 2 ss 2(i), 18)`

GIVEN `it is bringing, defending or settling a claim or proceeding, or using legal services for one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to my money or property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Which kind of matter is my claim`
`sch 2 -- the kind of matter` `it is bringing, defending or settling a claim or proceeding, or using legal services for one` `it relates to my money or property` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is bringing, defending or settling a claim or proceeding, or using legal services for one`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it relates to my money or property`
         THEN JUST `a financial matter: a legal matter relating to your financial or property matters, for an administrator (sch 2 ss 1(o), 18)`
         ELSE JUST `a personal matter: a legal matter not relating to your financial or property matters, for a guardian (sch 2 ss 2(i), 18)`

@export Is my claim (bringing, defending or settling it) a financial matter, for an administrator, or a personal matter, for a guardian (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) sch 2 ss 1, 2, 18)? No answer means the matter is not one of the legal matters schedule 2 section 18 lists.
GIVEN `it is bringing, defending or settling a claim or proceeding, or using legal services for one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter bringing or defending a claim or proceeding (before a court, tribunal or other body), settling a claim, or using legal services for one?
      `it relates to my money or property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the claim relate to your money or property (for example a claim for damages or compensation to be paid to you)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Which kind of matter is my claim`
DECIDE `Which kind of matter is my claim question` IS
    `sch 2 -- the kind of matter` `it is bringing, defending or settling a claim or proceeding, or using legal services for one` `it relates to my money or property`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `Schedule 4 -- paid carer`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- Sch 4: "paid carer, for an adult, means someone who-- (a) performs services for the adult's care; and (b) receives
-- remuneration from any source for the services, other than-- (i) a carer payment or other benefit received from the
-- Commonwealth or a State for providing home care for the adult; or (ii) remuneration attributable to the principle
-- that damages may be awarded by a court for voluntary services performed for the adult's care." A paid carer may not
-- be appointed (s 14(1)) and an appointee who becomes one loses the appointment (s 26(1)(a)). Limb (b)(ii): a family
-- carer whose care is paid for out of the adult's damages for gratuitous care is not a paid carer.
GIVEN `performs services for my care` IS A BOOLEAN
      `receives remuneration for the services apart from the two excluded kinds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch 4 -- paid carer` `performs services for my care` `receives remuneration for the services apart from the two excluded kinds` IF
        `performs services for my care`
    AND `receives remuneration for the services apart from the two excluded kinds`

@export Is the person who cares for me a "paid carer", which would stop them being my guardian or administrator (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) sch 4)? Money paid from my damages for their unpaid care does not count.
GIVEN `performs services for my care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person perform services for your care?
      `receives remuneration for the services apart from the two excluded kinds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person paid for that care from any source, apart from a government carer payment or benefit for home care, or money from damages awarded for voluntary care of you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my carer a paid carer question` IS
    `sch 4 -- paid carer` `performs services for my care` `receives remuneration for the services apart from the two excluded kinds`
